This is an experimental, unaffiliated
project that formalizes and investigates
arguments from Alessandro Maria Masullo’s
manuscript: The Music of the Primes.

The LICENSE file covers this project's
code, Lean proofs, and other content
expressly not from the manuscript which
is wholly the original work of Masullo.

This project uses patel.codes/godel, an
experimental abstraction beyond agentic
coding harness, to define self-improving
programs whose goal is to formalize the
manuscript in Lean 4 and substantiate
any repairs that might be required in a
manner that is respectful towards expert
human attention.

This project makes use of AI-assistance
heavily. The intention is that the files
in Proofs/{Props,Theorems} are the final
human attention surface.

Agent nodes in Gödel programs invoke yah;
deterministic nodes may use other executables.
See cmd/handoff/README.md for a standalone
historical handoff reading check.
